    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0872" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1949v03/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/6–1149:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of State, at Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-12T01:00:00-04:00">June 12, 1949—1
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Telac 77. Eyes Only for the Secretary. We
                    assume from your Actel 59<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d414-f1"/> that you have given your approval to NSC paper<anchor n="2" xml:id="d414-f2"/> as now
                    written and are not asking that NSC amend para
                        3<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi> along lines of Telac 60.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d414-f3"/> Request reply to reach
                    Dept not later than early Monday morning, if possible, to meet appointment with
                    President.</p>
                <pb facs="0873" n="832" xml:id="pg832"/>
                <p>Will inform NSC and President of two points
                    covered your Actel 59 and intensify efforts to
                    determine all feasible counter-measures.</p>
                <p>Will attempt to obtain modification of NSC paper
                    to make unmistakably clear your discretion re: warning to Soviets on imposition
                    of blockade. Have in mind an additional sentence in para five reading
                    approximately as follows: “It is considered however that the desirability of
                    making such a declaration in connection with the present meeting of the CFM as well as its textual content and manner of
                    presentation should be left to the discretion of the Secretary of State in the
                    light of the situation as it develops at the current meeting of the CFM.”<anchor n="4" xml:id="d414-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="1" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
